[profiles.guide]
notes = '''The right stick {rs} is a flick stick: push it to turn that way at once, then rotate it to keep turning. Gyro aims up, down and finely.
Gyro aims like the mouse. Hold {lb} and {rb} together to pause it while you reposition the controller, press {select} and {start} together to switch it off or on, and hold {l3} to recenter.
{rt} uses the tool in hand: place a part, swing the hammer, paint, connect, fire the spud gun. {lt} is its right-click (aim, erase, the lift's options); holding it also slows the right stick for aiming.
{west} uses and sits down, {south} jumps, {east} crouches (a toggle), {l3} sprints (a toggle). {rb} rotates the part you're placing, {r3} reloads.
Hold {lb} for the hotbar and pick a slot with the right stick {rs}; {left} and {right} step through it. In a seat, the hotbar slots are the seat's controls.
{north} opens the inventory and crafting, where the right stick {rs} moves the cursor and {rt} clicks. {up} is the map, {down} chat.
Hold {select} for the Driving mode once you sit in a seat: {rt} drives forward, {lt} back, {ls} steers. Hold {select} again to get back on your feet. {select} also lists the screens.
Naming a creation or chatting: {guide} + {west} opens the on-screen keyboard. The rotate, reload and map keys are inferred; check Options → Controls if one doesn't answer.'''

